From c2b7edb3347a48d4b7659164a444995511276b80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 06:40:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Shop category: the live list decides, and the admin can
 filter by it

Two things, one cause.

The shop resolved a product's category from a FIXED taxonomy compiled into the
build, while the admin panel resolved the same row from the `shop_categories`
table. Rename "Fragrance" to "Waxing products" and the two stop agreeing: the
panel counts the six products filed under that category (id or label match) and
the shop returns none of them, because a stored label that is not the seed
label falls through to the name rules and lands somewhere else. That is the
"admin says 6, website shows 0" report.

Now the live category list is part of the resolution, on both sides of the
filter: `resolveCategoryId` and the SQL CASE check the live ids and CURRENT
labels first (whitespace- and case-insensitively), then the seed label, then the
keyword rules. So a stored label resolves to its category exactly as the panel
counts it, and the count on the Categories tab and the shelf on the website are
one number by construction. The list is read through a 30-second cache and a
failure falls back to the seed taxonomy instead of failing the catalogue.

The second thing is the panel's new Category filter: `/admin-list` now accepts
the shop's own facets, so filtering the catalogue there asks the storefront's
question and gets the storefront's answer.

This patch SUPERSEDES `backend-shop-category-filter.patch`: it contains all of
that patch plus the live-list resolution. Apply one or the other, not both.
